{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\n\nOn 2026-11-11 a live agentic run of `us.meta.llama4-maverick-17b-instruct-v1:0` on Bedrock (us-west-2) with rebar's default `max_tokens` (`DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS = 16000`, src/rebar/llm/config.py) was rejected before generation: HTTP 400 ValidationException \"The maximum tokens you requested exceeds the model limit of 8192\". The same run with `max_tokens=8192` completed. Found while fixing garlicky-leery-seal.\n\n## Root cause (measured)\n\n- rebar already clamps each request's output cap to a per-model ceiling: `structured_run` takes `min(effective cap, _known_model_output_ceiling(model))`, read from the single-source table `MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS` in `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py` (the Nova entries were added the same way, bug cumulative-insensible-asianlion). The review paths also RAISE to that ceiling through `model_max_output_tokens`.\n- The table has no Llama 4 entry, so an unmapped Maverick keeps the 16000 default and Bedrock rejects every call.\n- Probed directly with boto3 Converse on 2026-11-12 02:49 PST (us-west-2, frontier-bedrock): `us.meta.llama4-maverick-17b-instruct-v1:0` and `us.meta.llama4-scout-17b-instruct-v1:0` both accept maxTokens 8192 (`end_turn`) and reject 8193 and 16000 with \"exceeds the model limit of 8192\".\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd `(\"llama4-maverick\", 8_192)` and `(\"llama4-scout\", 8_192)` to `MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS`, with a comment citing the measurement. The lookup is a substring match, so both the `us.` inference-profile ids and bare ids match. No config key, env var or flag; no other behaviour changes.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019.py`\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED then GREEN in `tests/unit/test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019.py`:\n  - `model_max_output_tokens` returns 8192 for `bedrock:us.meta.llama4-maverick-17b-instruct-v1:0`, `us.meta.llama4-scout-17b-instruct-v1:0` and the bare ids (fails pre-fix: 16000).\n  - The structured-run request settings for Maverick with the default 16000 cap carry `max_tokens == 8192` (the clamp path every run uses; fails pre-fix).\n  - The existing Claude, Nova and unmapped-model rows are unchanged.\n- Live: one PydanticAIRunner run of Maverick on Bedrock with the DEFAULT `max_tokens` completes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A test that fails on the pre-fix tree shows Llama 4 Maverick and Scout resolve to an 8192 output ceiling.\n- [ ] A test that fails on the pre-fix tree shows a Maverick request built from the default 16000 cap is sent with max_tokens 8192.\n- [ ] Existing ceiling rows (Claude, Nova, unmapped fallback) are unchanged, shown by the existing tests passing.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A live PydanticAIRunner run of `us.meta.llama4-maverick-17b-instruct-v1:0` on Bedrock with the default max_tokens completes, recorded as a comment.\n  provenance: environment=Bedrock us-west-2 via the frontier-bedrock profile from the fix-gecko worktree; principal=frontier-bedrock IAM identity; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — one runner call\n- [ ] [non-codebase] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.\n  provenance: environment=macOS dev host, fix-gecko worktree; principal=Rebar Bot Nava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — exit status and log live outside the repository\n"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794480622729934001,"uuid":"8d65c1c9-e3f9-4ea4-8f21-e8c8093fb3e3"}